{
  "summary": "Updates the Windows codesigning script in `contrib/` to pass the private key passphrase to `osslsigncode` via standard input rather than as a command-line argument. Using `printf` into `-readpass -` prevents the passphrase from appearing in process listings.",
  "problem": "During detached signature generation, `osslsigncode` receives the key passphrase via the `-pass` argument, exposing sensitive signing credentials in process arguments visible to any user or monitoring tool via `ps`.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'osslsigncode -pass places the key passphrase in the process arguments, so ps can read it.'",
    "Linked issue #36651: 'contrib: detached-sig-create.sh passes the signing passphrases as arguments'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "A minimal 3-line modification to signing tooling in contrib.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Pipes the Windows codesigning passphrase to osslsigncode via standard input instead of command-line arguments in contrib detached signing tooling. Currently, the script passes the passphrase via -pass, exposing it to process monitoring tools like ps on the signing host. This partially addresses issue #36651 using osslsigncode's -readpass - option.",
